    "title": "South Carolina women's basketball vs Oklahoma in March Madness Sweet 16 live news, bracket predictions, how to watch",
    "text": "March 26, 2026, 6:06 a.m. ETSouth Carolina women's basketball faces Oklahoma in an all-SEC showdown in March Madness Sweet 16 on March 28 in Sacramento.The Gamecocks and Sooners played in one of the best games of the regular season on Jan. 22, a 94-82 Oklahoma victory in overtime in Norman. The loss was South Carolina's lone defeat in SEC play.Joyce Edwards, the Gamecocks leading scorer, had two 20-point games in the first weekend of the NCAA Tournament.Oklahoma's Raegan Beers posted two double-doubles as the Sooners advanced to the Sweet 16. When does South Carolina women's basketball play in the Sweet 16?The South Carolina Gamecocks and Oklahoma Sooners will play at 5 p.m. ET, Saturday, March 28, 2026. What channel is South Carolina women's basketball vs Oklahoma game on?The South Carolina Gamecocks and Oklahoma Sooners will air on ESPN on Saturday, March 28, 2026. South Carolina vs Oklahoma March Madness predictions, picksGreenville News reporter Lulu Kesin's pick: South Carolina 96, Oklahoma 80The Gamecocks beat Vanderbilt by 29 fresh off the Oklahoma loss and key players for Staley seem to be in better spots now than they were in the first matchup. This team wants revenge and scored 204 points across the first two rounds.And from the USA TODAY desk:Nancy Armour: South CarolinaHeather Burns: South CarolinaMeghan L. Hall: South CarolinaCydney Henderson: South CarolinaMitchell Northam: South Carolina South Carolina vs Oklahoma oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM.Spread: South Carolina -18.5 (-105), Oklahoma +18.5 (-115)Total: 153.5; Under -110, Over -110Moneyline: South Carolina -2500, Oklahoma +1100 South Carolina, Oklahoma women's basketball injury updatesSouth Carolina has had injury issues all season, starting with Chloe Kitts' torn ACL suffered in September.Adhel Tac has not played since Feb. 5 with a lower-body injury.Maddy McDaniel missed the first round game against Southern with an illness and played just two minutes vs. USC. Sweet 16 bracket, schedule2026 NCAA tournament Sweet 16 March Madness games Friday, March 27Regional 1 -- Fort Worth: 2-seed Vanderbilt vs. 6-seed Notre Dame, 2:30 p.m. on ESPNRegional 1 -- Fort Worth: 1-seed UConn vs. 4-seed UNC, 5 p.m. on ESPNRegional 2 -- Sacramento: 1-seed UCLA vs. 4-seed Minnesota, 7:30 p.m. on ESPNRegional 2 -- Sacramento: 2-seed LSU vs. 3-seed Duke, 10 p.m. on ESPN2026 NCAA tournament Sweet 16 March Madness games Saturday, March 28Regional 3 -- Fort Worth: 2-seed Michigan vs. 3-seed Louisville, 12:30 p.m. on ABCRegional 3 -- Fort Worth: 1-seed Texas vs. 5-seed Kentucky, 3 p.m. on ABCRegional 4 -- Sacramento: 1-seed South Carolina vs. 4-seed Oklahoma, 5 p.m. on ESPNRegional 4 -- Sacramento: 3-seed TCU vs. 10-seed Virginia, 7:30 p.m. on ESPN South Carolina women's basketball March Madness results, South Carolina women's basketball NCAA Tournament game scoresSouth Carolina overwhelmed USC in the first quarter en route to a 101-61 victory in the second round on March 23. Joyce Edwards led all scorers with 23 points to go with 10 rebounds.In the first round, the Gamecocks coasted to a 103-34 victory over Southern in the first round on March 21. Edwards had 27 points and eight rebounds, while Tessa Johnson added 14 points, 10 rebounds and five assists. Oklahoma women's basketball March Madness results, score of OU women's basketball games in NCAA TournamentThe Sooners overcame a halftime deficit to beat Michigan State 77-71 on March 22 in the second round. Raegan Beers led the way with 18 points, 14 rebounds, four steals and two blocks.Oklahoma sprinted out to a lead early and walked away with a 89-59 victory over Idaho on March 20 in the first round. South Carolina vs Oklahoma women's basketball historyOklahoma leads the all-time series 4-2, with the Sooners winning the teams' matchup this season in overtime on Jan. 22.This season's Sweet 16 matchup will be the two teams' first NCAA Tournament matchup. Who are South Carolina's best players? South Carolina women's basketball roster00, G Ta'Niya Latson1, G Maddy McDaniel5, G Tessa Johnson8, F Joyce Edwards11, C Madina Okot15, F Adhel Tac21, F Chloe Kitts24, G Ayla McDowell25, G Raven Johnson30, F Maryam Dauda31, F Alicia Tournebize44, G Agot Makeer Who is South Carolina women's basketball coach? Dawn Staley is all-time great, leading another title contenderDawn Staley's coaching career began while she was an WNBA player.Staley took over as Temple's head coach in 2000, and the Owls quickly became a NCAA Tournament mainstay. Temple made the tournament six times in eight years with Staley in charge.Staley became South Carolina's head coach in 2008, slowly reviving the program. The Gamecocks first made the NCAA Tournament in 2012, Staley's fourth season, and have made the tournament every year since.The Gamecocks reached the Final Four for the first time in program history in 2015, then won the program's first national title in 2017.The Gamecocks are on an active five-year Final Four streak, a stretch that includes two national titles.Staley's South Carolina resume includes more than 500 career wins, three national championships and seven Final Four appearances. 2026 Oklahoma Sooners women's basketball roster0, C Beatrice Culliton2, G Aaliyah Chavez3, G Zya Vann4, F Caya Smith6, F Sahara Williams10, F Emma Tolan12, G Payton Verhulst15, C Raegan Beers21, F Brooklyn Stewart22, G Keziah Lofton26, C Daffa CIssokoWho is Oklahoma women's basketball coach? Jennie Baranczyk led Sooners to Sweet 16 in consecutive seasonsJennie Baranczyk played collegiately at Iowa, then started her coaching career after her playing career in 2004.After nine seasons as the Drake head coach, including three NCAA Tournament appearances, Baranczyk became OU's next head coach in 2021.The Sooners made the NCAA Tournament in each of Baranczyk's first five seasons. OU has reached the second weekend in 2025 and 2026.",
